WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.305 --> 00:00:02.164
- [Instructor] Breathing.

00:00:02.164 --> 00:00:04.022
- Oh, gosh. I think it's terrifying.

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:05.624
- I have no experience in boxing.

00:00:06.224 --> 00:00:08.433
- Alright, five seconds.
Move when I say go.

00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:10.152
Plant your feet. Hit me one, two

00:00:10.152 --> 00:00:11.162
- Aw, I gotta do that?

00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:11.944
- And ...

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:12.904
Go!

00:00:12.904 --> 00:00:15.824
- My experience with
boxing is very limited.

00:00:15.824 --> 00:00:18.658
- C.J.'s gonna make sure that
none of this gets destroyed.

00:00:18.658 --> 00:00:20.051
- I don't wanna mess this up.

00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:22.279
- Plant your feet. Jab, cross, jab, cross.

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:23.569
(laughs)

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:24.750
- I got my ass kicked in pilates,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.167
so this is going to be
challenging as well.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.583
- I really hope I don't pass out.

00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:28.674
- [Instructor] Time.

00:00:28.674 --> 00:00:29.441
- God.

00:00:29.441 --> 00:00:33.410
Whew. Okay.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.704
(calming music)

00:00:36.704 --> 00:00:38.519
- I've been boxing since
I was a little kid.

00:00:38.519 --> 00:00:40.725
A lot of people come into
boxing already in shape.

00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:43.209
The way you breath and
the way you push yourself

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.176
is a lot different than
in any other sport.

00:00:45.176 --> 00:00:47.064
Boxing really does push
you to different levels.

00:00:48.354 --> 00:00:49.465
We're going to get into
some technical drills

00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:52.026
on how to move, where to
punch, what punches what.

00:00:52.026 --> 00:00:53.491
Then we'll get into padwork drills,

00:00:53.491 --> 00:00:54.683
you guys are gonna hit some pads.

00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:55.653
(alarm sounds)

00:00:55.653 --> 00:00:56.643
- [Instructor] Let's go.

00:00:58.103 --> 00:01:00.590
- Yeah, I wanna be pounding
a piece of meat right now.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:01.390
(laughs)

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.560
- Grab, like, two
levers, you're gonna pull

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.180
those levers right in front of you.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.499
Okay. Now I'm gonna take my left foot,

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.458
slide it right out in front.

00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:09.887
Now, the first punch is our jab.

00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:11.512
It's the most important punch in boxing.

00:01:11.512 --> 00:01:13.068
The jab's gonna be our lead hand.

00:01:13.068 --> 00:01:14.507
It's gonna come out and rotate over.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.552
These two hurt what we're hitting,

00:01:16.552 --> 00:01:17.499
these two knuckles hurt us.

00:01:17.499 --> 00:01:18.985
We're just gonna bring
it and come right back,

00:01:18.985 --> 00:01:20.589
keep our legs bent the whole time. Ready?

00:01:20.589 --> 00:01:25.042
One, two, three, four.

00:01:25.042 --> 00:01:26.636
All right, so now we're
gonna go to the cross.

00:01:26.636 --> 00:01:27.781
The cross is the money punch.

00:01:27.781 --> 00:01:28.759
It's gonna come right from this side,

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:30.016
you're gonna push off your back leg.

00:01:30.016 --> 00:01:31.957
It's gonna come straight, aligned

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:34.418
from your knee to your
foot, and come right back.

00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:36.136
Instead of crossing this
way, I don't want you

00:01:36.136 --> 00:01:38.626
punching somebody's cousin,
uncle, sister, right?

00:01:38.626 --> 00:01:39.209
Punch the person right in front of you.

00:01:39.209 --> 00:01:40.099
- Okay.

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:43.856
- Ready? Three, four, much better, five.

00:01:43.856 --> 00:01:44.695
You see how now it gets that snap?

00:01:44.695 --> 00:01:45.205
- Yeah.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.879
- Okay, so in boxing, there's numbers

00:01:46.879 --> 00:01:48.309
associated with punching.

00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:50.106
A jab is a one, a cross is a two.

00:01:50.106 --> 00:01:54.077
Two, one. One two. Jab.

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:55.468
Ahh, good.

00:01:55.468 --> 00:01:56.098
(laughs)

00:01:56.098 --> 00:01:56.678
We're gonna go non-stop

00:01:56.678 --> 00:01:58.086
for the next thirty
seconds, this right here.

00:01:58.086 --> 00:01:59.689
Let's go. Breathe, breathe, breathe,

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:01.593
breathe, breathe. There you go.

00:02:03.503 --> 00:02:03.891
Time.

00:02:03.891 --> 00:02:04.747
(alarm sounds)

00:02:04.747 --> 00:02:06.816
All right, so now we're gonna
work on how to move our feet.

00:02:06.816 --> 00:02:08.133
- Does anybody else have this puddle?

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.043
(laughs)

00:02:09.043 --> 00:02:12.734
- Resetting, resetting, resetting. Good.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.336
Continuously let your weight feel

00:02:14.336 --> 00:02:16.193
in your legs, and go backwards.

00:02:16.193 --> 00:02:17.092
- I feel like I could sneak up

00:02:17.092 --> 00:02:18.531
on someone and really
give them the hammer.

00:02:18.531 --> 00:02:20.202
- I don't even think
we're through the warm-up,

00:02:20.202 --> 00:02:21.544
and I'm like, already tired.

00:02:23.011 --> 00:02:24.236
- When the bell beeps, it's gonna

00:02:24.236 --> 00:02:25.513
give us a 30-second warning.

00:02:25.513 --> 00:02:26.836
So, you're gonna to go
non-stop on the bag.

00:02:26.836 --> 00:02:27.938
It's not about pushing it, it's just

00:02:27.938 --> 00:02:29.908
about non-stop movement.

00:02:29.908 --> 00:02:30.933
One, two, three, four.

00:02:30.933 --> 00:02:31.783
- [Girl] Oh!
- [Instructor] Yep.

00:02:31.783 --> 00:02:32.713
- Okay.

00:02:32.713 --> 00:02:35.757
One, two, three, four, jab, jab,

00:02:35.757 --> 00:02:40.070
jab, cross, jab cross, backup, backup.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.812
- I feel kinda like a badass.

00:02:41.812 --> 00:02:42.792
- Non-stop, go!

00:02:42.792 --> 00:02:45.715
(punching sounds)

00:02:48.215 --> 00:02:49.082
(alarm sounds)

00:02:49.082 --> 00:02:50.680
- She had a strong jab and a strong cross,

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.624
but we'll see what the guys have.

00:02:52.624 --> 00:02:53.864
- [Instructor] What knuckles
should you hit with?

00:02:53.864 --> 00:02:54.479
- Top, so I can snap it off.

00:02:54.479 --> 00:02:56.599
- [Instructor] There you go.

00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:59.803
Again, again, again.

00:02:59.803 --> 00:03:02.687
Jab, jab, cross. Backup.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.309
Ten seconds.

00:03:06.429 --> 00:03:08.471
- I hate you, Dad. I hate you.

00:03:08.471 --> 00:03:09.169
(alarm sounds)

00:03:09.169 --> 00:03:10.387
- [Instructor] Time.

00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:17.690
(punching sounds)

00:03:22.733 --> 00:03:26.530
- They're good. They all actually
have a good punch on 'em,

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.512
but hers actually has more pop than them.

00:03:29.512 --> 00:03:31.242
(laughs)

00:03:31.242 --> 00:03:33.525
- Holla!

00:03:33.525 --> 00:03:35.920
I'm gonna beat their
asses. Just watch out.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.126
- My arms are turning into noodles,

00:03:38.126 --> 00:03:42.134
so it's challenging. It's
different than pilates.

00:03:42.134 --> 00:03:44.416
- It's okay. Not everybody
can handle it, it's all right.

00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:45.972
- [Instructor] Grab your
jump rope. All right, ready?

00:03:45.972 --> 00:03:47.522
Fast feet, go. Fast feet. Hands up.

00:03:47.522 --> 00:03:49.360
Fast feet. Speed. Speed.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.819
And push ups, go. Push ups.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:52.452
- What? Oh my God.

00:03:52.452 --> 00:03:54.401
- From the push ups to this,
we're going mountain climbing.

00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:55.101
Speed, let's go.

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:55.778
- [Voiceover] Oh, fuck me!

00:03:55.778 --> 00:03:57.604
- Let's go. Let's go.

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:00.473
Three, two, one ...

00:04:01.605 --> 00:04:02.120
Time.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.211
(claps)

00:04:05.461 --> 00:04:08.308
- I'm thoroughly beat. My feet hurt, too.

00:04:08.308 --> 00:04:09.664
There's not anything
like it, really, though,

00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:10.254
- [in unison] Mm-mm.

00:04:10.254 --> 00:04:13.228
- It's cool, you guys did really
well, for your first class.

00:04:13.228 --> 00:04:15.156
- Can you say that one more
time, please? Into the camera?

00:04:15.156 --> 00:04:16.479
- These two did really well.

00:04:16.479 --> 00:04:17.625
You know, it teaches you how to

00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:18.922
push through things when you're tired.

00:04:18.922 --> 00:04:20.761
It teaches you how to achieve goals

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:22.168
that you didn't know that were possible.

00:04:22.168 --> 00:04:24.302
Boxing, it's not good
just for physical fitness,

00:04:24.302 --> 00:04:26.440
but just understanding how much

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.779
more about yourself you can learn.

00:04:27.779 --> 00:04:30.246
(upbeat music)

